  "kanji": "湿",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 湿\ntitle: damp, moist\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 12\nradical: 水\nradicalNumber: 85\nonyomi: [シツ, シュウ]\nkunyomi: [しめ.る, しめ.す, うるお.う, うるお.す]\ndistractors: [温, 昇, 泊]\n---\n\n# 湿 — damp, moist\n\n**Strokes:** 12 · **Key (radical):** 水 (no. 85) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n湿 expresses dampness, moisture, or humidity. The native verbs distinguish becoming damp from wetting something.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Picture moisture collecting below the upper box and among the spreading lower strokes on the right, beside the water radical.\n\nThe indexing radical 水 appears as 氵 at the left.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| シツ | on | [湿度](../words/湿度.md) しつど - humidity; [湿気](../words/湿気.md) しっけ / しっき - moisture; humidity |\n| シュウ | on | Source-only reading; see the qualification below. |\n| しめ.る | kun | [湿る](../words/湿る.md) しめる - become damp; become moist |\n| しめ.す | kun | 湿す しめす - wet; moisten something |\n| うるお.う | kun | Source-only reading; see the qualification below. |\n| うるお.す | kun | Source-only reading; see the qualification below. |\n\nKANJIDIC2 also records `シュウ`, `うるお.う`, `うるお.す`. No suitable word example was established in the inspected JMdict snapshot. These are character-dictionary readings for lookup, not recommendations to use this kanji as an everyday spelling of a word.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [湿度](../words/湿度.md) しつど - humidity\n- [湿気](../words/湿気.md) しっけ / しっき - moisture; humidity\n- [湿る](../words/湿る.md) しめる - become damp; become moist\n\n## Notes\n\n- [湿る](../words/湿る.md) しめる is intransitive godan, not ichidan: 湿って しめって. 湿す しめす is transitive godan.\n- 湿度 measures moisture in the air; it is not another word for temperature.\n- The source-only うるお.う and うるお.す rows do not justify changing the spelling of an everyday word merely because its pronunciation matches.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1320370, 1320390, 1320410, 1320490.\n",
